BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Section 4: Firsthand Failure Modes, Traps & Economics Checks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 693.77 Tm (TJackk and partner Camila's first renter was the textbook trap: a needy driver who leaned on a family story, got a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 678.55 Tm (lowered rate, then had a string of things slide that should never have slid, and it ended up biting them [4NPuQA-V4ZA) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 663.32 Tm (@ 00:02:04]. The same renter had bought an Uber Black account, never said so, and when the pair tried to attach that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 648.10 Tm (driver to the fleet the dashboard kept flagging 'action needed'; they spent the whole time angry at Uber when the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 632.87 Tm (account was the problem [4NPuQA-V4ZA @ 00:02:52]. The fix was cold Enterprise logic: nobody rents a $600 car to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 617.65 Tm (someone holding $50, so it is now limousine license and money up front, no 'I'll pay you later' deals, and young owners) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 602.42 Tm (should expect older renters to test them [4NPuQA-V4ZA @ 00:05:48]. Rideshare Professor enforces behavior after the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 587.20 Tm (keys leave: tracking apps show whether a driver is pushing over 80, or rushing back at 100 miles an hour late at night,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 571.97 Tm (and the rule is one warning, then out; firing one or two drivers makes the rest play by the book [4Y5_eWf85tM @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 556.75 Tm (00:13:13]. Leniency is the expensive habit both camps had to kill.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.52 Tm (Repairs hit in clusters. TJackk lost two SUVs in a single week: a bad coolant leak on the Range Rover cost $5,000, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (the Ford Expedition blew catalytic converters on both the right and left sides, roughly $7,000 out the door in under) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (seven days, and without that cash the fleet would have sat earning nothing [UTnHLaPqh1s @ 00:03:16]. That is why) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (TJackk separates cash flow from profit: an SUV can cash flow $1,000 a week, but emergencies, upkeep, the car note,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (and insurance come out first, and whatever survives is the real number [9mwQox6xtqw @ 00:03:28]. Rideshare) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm (Professor handles downtime on the rent side: a car in the shop for half a week on an $800 weekly rate bills the driver) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm ($400, and tires or a transmission at 150,000 miles get pro-rated rather than fought over, because the priority is getting) Tj ET
