BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 493.77 Tm (The most expensive trap is the insurance gap. Etienne Elsaesser lays it out: platform commercial coverage only applies) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 478.55 Tm (while the driver is logged in, on-trip third-party liability through Hugo only pays when the renter hits someone else,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 463.32 Tm (and a $4K car totaled in week one gets eaten by the owner because the deposit will never cover it, a blind spot most) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 448.10 Tm (operators only learn the hard way [amfsF8yd5hg @ 00:04:22]. RevHostHQ's 'Sam' scenario shows the same hole from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 432.87 Tm (the compliance side: a cash handshake with a driver risks deactivation and leaves the car uninsured, so the fix is an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 417.65 Tm (approved route, a card on file, a check of the driver's insurance, and a weekly inspection [3jfvZ2LM8zM @ 00:01:26].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 402.42 Tm (Even Kell King, who self-insures and leans on a commercial liability policy for street compliance, concedes under) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 387.20 Tm (questioning that the commercial policy is typically not going to pay out when an uninsured renter causes the loss) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 371.97 Tm ([5liDEdRcRhY @ 00:44:12]. The Kel King channel adds hard lines of its own: never run these cars on a personal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 356.75 Tm (policy, pair GPS with a kill switch, and back every handoff with a signed agreement and a deposit while checking local) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 341.52 Tm (rules such as California smog testing [swveqE_MJY0 @ 00:07:23].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 326.30 Tm (Payment and recovery failures come next. Alex Auto warns that Uber and Lyft account screenshots can be faked, so) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 311.07 Tm (even with the platforms already running background and MVR checks, that operation still runs its own background) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 295.85 Tm (check and license verification rather than trusting the platform's screening alone [UJnOivSethI @ 00:04:00]. King of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 280.62 Tm (Rentals is blunter about money in motion: do not take a Zelle payment and take the renter's word for it, because 'you) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 265.40 Tm (will lose 99% of the time' [qwQ8yQbhunw @ 01:09:58]. Recovery hardware is treated as mandatory rather than) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 250.17 Tm (optional. Yanni, interviewed on darius benders after four years of renting cars to Uber drivers in Michigan, runs two) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 234.95 Tm (trackers per car and sometimes three, each tied to a remote cut-off [NFLtPz5bUp4 @ 00:13:20]. Etienne Elsaesser) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 219.72 Tm (specs hardwired units such as Move Tracks, Trackhawk, or Fleet Bolt with a kill switch, budgets a couple hundred) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 204.50 Tm (dollars per device and install plus a monthly fee, and repossesses once a renter runs 24 to 48 hours late [amfsF8yd5hg) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 189.27 Tm (@ 00:07:58]. Across all four operators, verification that rests on a screenshot, a payment-app promise, or a single) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 174.05 Tm (tracker is exactly where cars and cash leak out of the fleet, so the controls get installed and enforced before the first) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 158.82 Tm (week is ever collected.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 143.60 Tm (The last checks are pure arithmetic. King of Rentals holds up 'The General,' an operator carrying $1M of debt against) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 128.37 Tm ($750K of cars, as the over-leverage warning every scaling fleet should study, and pairs it with the rule to always have) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 113.15 Tm (an exit plan when buying cars [qwQ8yQbhunw @ 00:58:19]. Alex Auto shows why financed cars bleed in this model:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 97.92 Tm (a $20K Camry driven 3,000 to 4,000 miles a month is worth under $10K after a single year [Sukdr8-ecMM @) Tj ET
